--
N5008 [expr.cast]/2 + [dcl.ambig.res]: `(wp)' can only start a cast if `wp'
names a type; here it names a data member, so `*(wp) & m' is
`(*wp) & m' -- the parenthesized name is a primary expression.  The front
end parses it as the dereference of `(wp) & m' ("operator 'bitand' not
defined for types 'unsigned long int *' and 'unsigned long int'") when the
parenthesized name is a MEMBER used inside a member function -- the same
expression on a local pointer in a free function is fine.  This is
libstdc++'s bitset::reference::operator~ and operator bool (bitset:908 and
913, 6 cbmc-cpp descs in the round-163 audit): every `b[i]' read of a
std::bitset is nondet.  Header-free.  Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot
bin51 fails the same way).
